 "comment": "Vouchers sharing a GUID; every amount is a multiple of 10000 paise. Wages is listed; Cartage, Job Work and Hamali are mapped 194C. dup-a: ALPHA TRADERS (A1) and BETA STORES (A2), each with a handle of its own: two rows, each citing dup-a. dup-b: GAMMA MILLS (B1) and a payment whose narration is not read (B2). dup-c: DELTA WORKS twice; C1 also debits Driver Advances 200000 and C2, a Contra, does too: one row of two payments, citing dup-c twice (two labels), and its payee_elsewhere figure counts C1 only. dup-d: EPSILON CARRIERS twice with one type, number and day: two payments, one citation. Two vouchers with no GUID pay ZETA: two payments, cited under an empty id. dup-e: a Job Work bill credited to a creditor (E1), a Cartage payment of 3500000 to ETA (E2) and a cancelled Hamali bill (E3). The TDS payee test's finding cites dup-e for E2; Cartage is added, and so is Job Work, debited on E1 under the same GUID (E1 is in not_through_bank_total); Hamali, on the cancelled voucher, is not. dup-f: THETA (F1) and a cancelled payment (F2). The book check POP-5 reports the five shared GUIDs and the blank one; the result check POP-4 reports the four citations of dup-e and the one of dup-f, GUIDs a cancelled voucher also carries. The module check reads the last regular voucher of a GUID and fires NP-2 for dup-a (ALPHA TRADERS' citation resolves to BETA STORES' payment) and for dup-b (to the unread one, tag none), NP-3 for dup-a, NP-4 (BETA STORES in two rows), NP-5 (the handle BETA.S in two rows) and NP-7 (the Contra C2 counts for nothing, against 200000).",
